From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zetarancio <zetarancio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] devfreq: rockchip: add RK3568 DMC devfreq driver

Add a DMC (Dynamic Memory Controller) devfreq driver for the
RK3566/RK3568 SoCs.

DDR frequency scaling on these SoCs uses a shared-memory protocol
with the ARM Trusted Firmware (ATF version >= 0x102):

  1. Kernel requests a shared page via SIP_SHARE_MEM.
  2. Kernel writes the target frequency (Hz) to the shared page.
  3. SET_RATE SIP call returns -6 ("started, wait for MCU").
  4. Kernel starts the on-chip MCU via MCU_START SIP sub-command.
  5. MCU performs the hardware frequency change and fires GIC SPI 10.
  6. IRQ handler calls POST_SET_RATE for cleanup.

The completion interrupt's hardware IRQ number is written into the
shared page so ATF can signal completion on the correct GIC line.

Voltage scaling follows standard devfreq OPP practices: raise voltage
before scaling up, lower voltage after scaling down.

During suspend the driver restores the boot-time DDR frequency (as
expected by the ATF resume path) and enables DDR auto self-refresh for
lower power consumption.

Signed-off-by: Zetarancio <zetarancio@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/devfreq/Kconfig                |  13 +
 drivers/devfreq/Makefile               |   1 +
 drivers/devfreq/rk3568_dmc.c           | 593 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sip.h    |  11 +
 4 files changed, 618 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/devfreq/rk3568_dmc.c

